abstract: >-
  OpenIDEA Kiro is a Spec-Driven Development (SDD) tooling ecosystem and OpenIDEA
  IDE plugin that introduces formal requirement constraints, domain ontology
  grounding, and sub-millisecond logical contradiction detection to software
  engineering lifecycles. By pairing Easy Approach to Requirements Syntax (EARS)
  with project-level ontologies and Reduced Ordered Binary Decision Diagrams
  (ROBDDs) via biodivine-lib-bdd, Kiro finitizes discrete domain states and
  continuous integer thresholds into canonical decision diagrams. This provides
  O(1) satisfiability verification, exact minimal counterexample witness extraction,
  and guaranteed resource bounds within a zero-dependency WebAssembly (wasm32-wasip2)
  plugin runtime and native CI quality gate.
